WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.972 --> 00:00:06.405
In this walkthrough, we replace logos used in a sidebar and check that they fit before saving.

2
00:00:06.405 --> 00:00:08.715
This matters because oversized logos make sidebars look uneven and force editors to fix layout problems after upload. Preparing the right dimensions first makes the sidebar much easier to maintain.

3
00:00:08.715 --> 00:00:10.516
Open a page editor that contains the Sidebar widget and its logo content.

4
00:00:10.516 --> 00:00:13.051
Expand the Sidebar slot to reveal the logo-related widget rows.

5
00:00:13.051 --> 00:00:15.162
Use the plus icon on Sidebar to add or replace a logo/image widget in the correct slot.

6
00:00:15.162 --> 00:00:17.405
Choose Image widget for a logo file. Prepare logos around 480 px wide so they display sharply at about 240 px.

7
00:00:17.405 --> 00:00:20.603
Click the settings icon on the Image widget row.

8
00:00:20.603 --> 00:00:24.483
Use the widget settings to name and replace the sidebar logo content before saving.

9
00:00:24.483 --> 00:00:26.815
After this walkthrough, you should know where sidebar logos are edited, what size to prepare, and how to preview the result.
